          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            For a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-monad"} 2-monad
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mi Alg
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T Alg
            of
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed "-morphisms" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-limits"} 2-limits
            (bilimits), and more precisely
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pie-limits"} pie-limits
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %msub
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi l
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T Alg_l
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %msub
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T Alg_c
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+morphism"} lax and colax
            = succeed "-morphisms" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rigged+limit"} rigged limit
            for a characterization of these. There is no 2-category containing both lax and colax morphisms, but nevertheless some limits of diagrams involving lax and colax morphisms can be given a
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comma+object"} comma object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f/g)
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is colax and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            is lax. It is unclear exactly how to state a universal property for this comma object, but it is probably related to the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+category+of+algebras"} double category of algebras
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            be a (strict, for simplicity)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-monad"} 2-monad
            on a (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-category"}> strict
            , for simplicity)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:A\to C
            be a colax
            = succeed "-morphism" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo :
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g:B\to C
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+morphism"} lax
            = succeed "-morphism." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-limit"} strict
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comma+object"} comma object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f/g)
            exists in
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p:(f/g)\to A
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q:(f/g)\to B
            (which are, so far, only morphisms in
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi p
                        %mtd
                          %mi A
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo
                            %mi q
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ⇙
                            %mi α
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mi f
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi B
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi g
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{ (f/g) &amp; \xrightarrow{p} &amp; A\\
                  ^q\downarrow &amp; \swArrow_\alpha &amp; \downarrow^f \\
                  B &amp; \xrightarrow{g} &amp; C
                  }
          %p
            that is universal among such 2-cells. Now consider the following
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting+diagram"} pasting composite
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi T
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi T
                          %mi A
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ⇙
                            %mrow
                              %mi T
                              %mi α
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mrow
                              %mi T
                              %mi f
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi T
                          %mi B
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi T
                          %mi C
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ⇙
                            %mover
                              %mi f
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                        %mtd
                          %mi A
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ⇙
                            %mover
                              %mi g
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mi f
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi B
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi g
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  T(f/g) &amp; \to &amp; T A \\
                  \\downarrow &amp; \swArrow_{T\alpha} &amp; \downarrow^{T f} &amp; \searrow \\
                  T B &amp; \to &amp; T C &amp; \swArrow_{\bar{f}} &amp; A \\
                  \&amp; \searrow &amp; \swArrow_{\bar{g}} &amp; \searrow &amp;\downarrow^f \\
                  \&amp;&amp; B &amp; \xrightarrow{g} &amp; C
                  }
          %p
            Here
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar{f}
            is the colax
            = succeed "-morphism" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar{g}
            is the lax
            = succeed "-morphism" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f/g)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(f/g) \to (f/g)
            such that the above pasting composite is equal to the following one:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi T
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi T
                          %mi A
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi T
                          %mi B
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi A
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ⇙
                            %mi α
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mi f
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi B
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi g
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  T(f/g) &amp; \to &amp; T A \\
                  \\downarrow &amp; \searrow &amp;  &amp; \searrow \\
                  T B &amp; &amp; (f/g) &amp; \to &amp; A \\
                  \&amp; \searrow &amp; \downarrow &amp; \swArrow_\alpha &amp;\downarrow^f \\
                  \&amp;&amp; B &amp; \xrightarrow{g} &amp; C
                  }
          %p
            where the empty quadrilaterals commute. A similar argument shows that this map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(f/g) \to (f/g)
            is the action map of a
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f/g)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p:(f/g)\to A
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q:(f/g)\to B
            are strict
            = succeed "-morphisms" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            is a 2-cell in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+category+of+algebras"} double category of algebras
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Alg
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \mathbf{Alg}
          %p
            The strictness of the projections
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo ,
                  %mi q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p,q
            is familiar from the behavior of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rigged+limits"} rigged limits
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %msub
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi l
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T Alg_l
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T Alg_c
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f/g)
            has, although it seems likely to involve the double category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Alg
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \mathbf{Alg}
            somehow.
